## Disaster Recovery

### Backup Strategy

```bash
#!/bin/bash
# backup-temporal.sh

TIMESTAMP=$(date +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S)
BACKUP_DIR="/backups/temporal"

# Backup PostgreSQL
pg_dump -h $POSTGRES_HOST -U temporal temporal_default > \
  $BACKUP_DIR/temporal_${TIMESTAMP}.sql

# Backup Elasticsearch (visibility)
elasticdump \
  --input=http://elasticsearch:9200/temporal_visibility_v1_default \
  --output=$BACKUP_DIR/elasticsearch_${TIMESTAMP}.json

# Upload to S3
aws s3 cp $BACKUP_DIR/ s3://temporal-backups/ --recursive

# Retain backups for 30 days
find $BACKUP_DIR -name "*.sql" -mtime +30 -delete
find $BACKUP_DIR -name "*.json" -mtime +30 -delete
```

### Restore Procedure

```bash
#!/bin/bash
# restore-temporal.sh

BACKUP_FILE=$1

# Restore PostgreSQL
psql -h $POSTGRES_HOST -U temporal temporal_default < $BACKUP_FILE

# Restore Elasticsearch
elasticdump \
  --input=$BACKUP_FILE \
  --output=http://elasticsearch:9200/temporal_visibility_v1_default
```

